<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav October inflation 1.4 pct vs 1.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav October inflation 1.4 pct vs 1.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INFLATION	  Oct 96     Sept 96	Oct 95</p>
<p> monthly RPI index rise    +  1.4     +  1.2	+ 10.0</p>
<p> yr/yr pct change	    + 69.6     + 83.8	  N.A.</p>
<p>NOTES -- Cumulative Jan-Oct inflation stood at 49.2 percent on December 1995.</p>
<p>Figures refer to rump Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>National Bank of Yugoslavia imposed a stabilisation programme on January 24, 1994, halting hyperinflation of 60 percent a day. -- Gordana Filipovic, Belgrade newsroom, +381 11 222 4254</p>
</text>
